WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.141
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:05.441 --> 00:00:09.048
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.348 --> 00:00:16.052
Unit twenty-eight: Relative Clauses (who / which / that). Today you will describe people and things with relative clauses.

4
00:00:16.352 --> 00:00:18.947
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:23.388
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:24.868
Who.

7
00:00:25.883 --> 00:00:27.500
Who means used for people.

8
00:00:28.083 --> 00:00:29.816
The man who lives here is kind.

9
00:00:30.417 --> 00:00:32.802
Your turn. Say: Who.

10
00:00:35.667 --> 00:00:36.366
Who.

11
00:00:37.117 --> 00:00:37.944
Which.

12
00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:41.124
Which means used for things and animals.

13
00:00:41.717 --> 00:00:43.403
The book which I read is good.

14
00:00:44.017 --> 00:00:46.530
Your turn. Say: Which.

15
00:00:49.367 --> 00:00:50.182
Which.

16
00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:51.604
That.

17
00:00:52.617 --> 00:00:54.709
That means used for people or things.

18
00:00:55.317 --> 00:00:57.014
The bag that I lost was blue.

19
00:00:57.617 --> 00:01:00.373
Your turn. Say: That.

20
00:01:03.233 --> 00:01:04.002
That.

21
00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:06.204
Relative pronoun.

22
00:01:07.217 --> 00:01:10.946
Relative pronoun means a word that begins a relative clause.

23
00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:13.224
Who is a relative pronoun.

24
00:01:13.817 --> 00:01:16.748
Your turn. Say: Relative pronoun.

25
00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:21.124
Relative pronoun.

26
00:01:21.883 --> 00:01:22.722
Person.

27
00:01:23.717 --> 00:01:25.589
Person means a human being.

28
00:01:26.183 --> 00:01:27.695
She is a kind person.

29
00:01:28.283 --> 00:01:30.912
Your turn. Say: Person.

30
00:01:33.767 --> 00:01:34.594
Person.

31
00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:36.038
Thing.

32
00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:39.166
Thing means an object or an idea.

33
00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:41.355
This is an interesting thing.

34
00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:44.312
Your turn. Say: Thing.

35
00:01:47.167 --> 00:01:47.947
Thing.

36
00:01:48.683 --> 00:01:50.068
Extra information.

37
00:01:51.083 --> 00:01:54.221
Extra information means more details about a noun.

38
00:01:54.817 --> 00:01:57.257
Extra information is between commas.

39
00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:01.280
Your turn. Say: Extra information.

40
00:02:04.133 --> 00:02:06.110
Extra information.

41
00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:08.269
Defining clause.

42
00:02:09.283 --> 00:02:12.885
Defining clause means a clause that tells us exactly which one.

43
00:02:13.483 --> 00:02:15.854
A defining clause identifies the noun.

44
00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:19.288
Your turn. Say: Defining clause.

45
00:02:22.133 --> 00:02:23.367
Defining clause.

46
00:02:24.167 --> 00:02:27.899
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:32.436
Visal, how can you describe your teacher? Use who.

48
00:02:33.550 --> 00:02:43.751
She is the teacher who helps me with English. A relative clause gives more information about a noun. Who is for people, which is for things, and that is for both.

49
00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:47.175
Does the clause tell us exactly which one?

50
00:02:48.283 --> 00:02:58.731
Yes, a defining clause does. The book which I bought is interesting. It tells us which book. We do not use commas with defining clauses.

51
00:02:59.817 --> 00:03:01.480
Can we leave the pronoun out?

52
00:03:02.583 --> 00:03:15.200
If the pronoun is the object, yes: The book I bought is good. If it is the subject, no: The man who lives here is kind. Do not repeat the subject: not 'who he lives'.

53
00:03:16.333 --> 00:03:17.810
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:22.681
Grammar focus: Relative clauses: who and which and that.

55
00:03:22.981 --> 00:03:24.157
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:27.128
The man who lives next door is a doctor.

57
00:03:28.017 --> 00:03:30.039
The book which I bought is interesting.

58
00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:32.857
This is the bag that I lost.

59
00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:41.470
Use who for people, which for things and that for both. A relative clause gives more information about a noun. Do not repeat the subject.

60
00:03:42.217 --> 00:03:46.088
Be careful! Don't say: The man who he lives here is old.

61
00:03:48.033 --> 00:03:50.428
Say: The man who lives here is old.

62
00:03:50.728 --> 00:03:52.286
Do not repeat the subject.

63
00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:55.729
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:56.533 --> 00:03:57.813
People and Things.

65
00:03:58.113 --> 00:04:00.612
The woman who teaches me English is very kind.

66
00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:04.099
The book which I read last week was interesting.

67
00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:07.274
This is the bag that I lost yesterday.

68
00:04:08.267 --> 00:04:10.800
A person who helps others is a good friend.

69
00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:14.334
A relative pronoun begins the clause.

70
00:04:15.433 --> 00:04:19.690
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:22.793
The girl blank sits next to me is Ana.

72
00:04:23.093 --> 00:04:26.213
A, who. B, which. C, what.

73
00:04:29.767 --> 00:04:31.627
The answer is A: who.

74
00:04:32.783 --> 00:04:34.377
The phone blank I bought is new.

75
00:04:34.677 --> 00:04:37.738
A, who. B, which. C, whose.

76
00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:42.940
The answer is B: which.

77
00:04:44.083 --> 00:04:46.896
Which pronoun is used for both people and things?

78
00:04:47.196 --> 00:04:50.837
A, who. B, which. C, that.

79
00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:56.283
The answer is C: that.

80
00:04:57.450 --> 00:04:58.997
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:59.297 --> 00:05:06.909
A, The man who he lives here is old.. B, The man who lives here is old.. C, The man which lives here is old..

82
00:05:10.467 --> 00:05:13.825
The answer is B: The man who lives here is old..

83
00:05:14.983 --> 00:05:18.260
According to the reading, who teaches the writer English?

84
00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:23.839
A, a kind woman. B, a doctor. C, a friend.

85
00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:29.446
The answer is A: a kind woman.

86
00:05:30.633 --> 00:05:33.634
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:34.483 --> 00:05:37.435
Describe a person or thing using who, which or that.

88
00:05:46.250 --> 00:05:47.727
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:48.027 --> 00:06:00.774
My friend is a person who always helps me. The book that I am reading is about an old castle. I use who for my friend and that for the book. A relative clause gives more information.

90
00:06:01.074 --> 00:06:02.899
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:03.783 --> 00:06:09.164
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and relative clauses: who and which and that.

92
00:06:09.464 --> 00:06:13.823
Today's value is communication. Speak clearly and listen carefully.

93
00:06:14.123 --> 00:06:16.938
See you in Unit twenty-nine. Goodbye!

94
00:06:17.238 --> 00:06:20.320
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

